+Independent classification judgment from the frozen source and supplied
+operational semantics
+
+  1. numericVal(V) = isInt(V) orBool isFloat(V): DEFINITION. It names the
+     Int-or-Float source-domain predicate.
+  2. numericVals(.ValSeq) = true: DEFINITION. Empty recurrence clause.
+  3. numericVals(vCons(V,REST)) = numericVal(V) andBool numericVals(REST):
+     DEFINITION. Structurally decreasing recurrence clause.
+  4. positiveNumeric(I:Int) = gtF(intToF(I),0.0): DEFINITION. Sort-specific
+     defining equation.
+  5. positiveNumeric(F:Float) = gtF(F,0.0): DEFINITION. Sort-specific
+     defining equation.
+  6. positiveNumeric(V:Val) = false outside numericVal: DEFINITION. Guarded
+     totalizing equation, disjoint from the two numeric cases.
+  7. filterPositive(ACC,.ValSeq) = ACC: DEFINITION. Empty recurrence clause.
+  8. positive-head filterPositive clause: DEFINITION. It appends the head and
+     recurs on REST.
+  9. nonpositive-head filterPositive clause: DEFINITION. It skips the head and
+     recurs on REST. The two guarded recursive clauses are complementary.
+ 10. applyCmp(">",V:Val,0.0) = positiveNumeric(V) when numericVal(V):
+     DOMAIN_LEMMA. It equates the supplied operational comparison symbol with
+     a proof-local summary. Supplied float.k defines the exact Int/Float
+     applyCmp cases; spec-connection.k proves specialized Int and Float
+     claims against VERIFICATION-BASE, but Stage 1 does not first prove this
+     exact generic rule and guard. It is therefore not PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA,
+     not a definition of applyCmp, and not an ordinary operational rule. It is
+     directly relevant to the source branch `x > 0.0` and the result filter.
+
+All four simplification rules are therefore either DEFINITION (rules 7-9) or
+DOMAIN_LEMMA (rule 10), as required.
