+  injection, the `numericVal(V) = true` guard, and equality to
+  `positiveNumeric(V)`. Those are precisely the LHS, guard, and RHS of
+  verification.k lines 43-45. There is no extra conjunct, duplicate, omitted
+  domain lemma, target relocation, or weakened conclusion. The guard is
+  satisfiable for both Int and Float constructors under the frozen defining
+  rules; its faithful implementation is checked again at the Stage 5 bridge.
